
================================================================
 SAVE FORMAT CHANGED -- EVERY EXISTING SAVED GAME WILL BE LOST
================================================================

  sizeof(struct Game) expected : 53362370 bytes  (packaging/ci/save-format-baseline)
  sizeof(struct Game) measured : 53383086 bytes  (this working tree)
  difference                   : 20716 bytes

A saved game is a raw dump of struct Game, and the engine loads one
only if its length equals sizeof(struct Game) for the running build
(src/game_saves.c). Something in this tree changed that size, so this
build CANNOT LOAD ANY SAVE written by any earlier build -- not the
player's campaigns, not their autosaves, not Continue.

WHAT TO DO

  Not intended?  Do not touch the baseline. Fix the change: keep the
                 new state out of struct Game, or reuse space that is
                 already there. Most fields that trip this only matter
                 at runtime and never needed saving.

  Intended?      Accept it deliberately -- in the same commit as the
                 change that caused it -- by editing
                 packaging/ci/save-format-baseline:

                     sizeof_struct_game=53383086

                 and saying in the commit message and CHANGELOG.md
                 that saves from earlier versions will not load. The
                 release notes get that warning automatically once the
                 baseline changes.

Read packaging/ci/save-format-baseline before deciding. This check is
never made green by editing it without one of the two answers above.
================================================================
